WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.264
- The last text message
my mom sent to me was

00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:04.530
"Did Beyonce have her babies yet?"

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.490
I said "I don't know." and she said

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.076
"You work at Buzzfeed,
for the love of God."

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:12.353
(playful music)

00:00:12.353 --> 00:00:14.963
- Costco had the most
beautiful hanging plants

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.973
so I had to get two, smiley face.

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:19.505
- Me and my mom are on a diet together,

00:00:19.505 --> 00:00:21.827
so the last thing she texted me is,

00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:24.254
"I am star-ving,

00:00:24.254 --> 00:00:26.736
I begged dad to get me a
Whopper from Burger King

00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:28.737
but he didn't, he's such an asshole."

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.570
- The last thing that my mom texted me

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.546
is a kiss-face emoji, and a heart emoji.

00:00:33.546 --> 00:00:36.144
- The last text my mom sent me is

00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:38.288
"Stay on our health insurance."

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:41.272
- The last thing my mom
texted me is that my parents

00:00:41.272 --> 00:00:44.372
got approved to adopt a dog named Hank!

00:00:44.372 --> 00:00:47.175
- The last thing my mom texted me was

00:00:47.175 --> 00:00:51.175
"I'm going to fire emoji, devil emoji."

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:53.471
So I'm going to hell.

00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:55.087
- My mom sent me a picture of her

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:57.607
and asked if her concealer was too light.

00:00:57.607 --> 00:00:59.662
- "Good morning, are you up yet?"

00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:02.806
- I asked her if she
would come to New York,

00:01:02.806 --> 00:01:04.839
and she was like "You
want me to visit you?"

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:08.212
and she was excited, and then I said

00:01:08.212 --> 00:01:10.509
"No, I want you to...

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:11.912
I want you to dog-sit."

00:01:11.912 --> 00:01:14.242
but she didn't respond
to that, so (laughs)

00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:15.769
I feel a little guilty.

00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:17.352
- The last thing my mom texted me

00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:19.842
was a picture of damage that my dad caused

00:01:19.842 --> 00:01:22.675
trying to DIY a dishwasher installation.

00:01:22.675 --> 00:01:24.595
And I said "Rough times."

00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:26.696
- Okay, so my mom recently texted me

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:30.011
the entire lyrics to the
songs Father &amp; Daughter

00:01:30.011 --> 00:01:34.115
by Paul Simon, literally the entire song.

00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:36.602
There it is, see it?

00:01:36.602 --> 00:01:37.733
Still going.

00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:39.632
- So the last text
message I got from my mom

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.005
was actually a smiley face,

00:01:41.005 --> 00:01:42.799
because she was thanking me on

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:44.801
being the biggest gift that she has,

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.082
and because I took her out for dinner

00:01:46.082 --> 00:01:48.723
for Guatemalan Mothers
Day, which is May 10th.

00:01:48.723 --> 00:01:50.941
- "Timmy was in the well again."

00:01:50.941 --> 00:01:53.193
My families one dog constantly escapes,

00:01:53.193 --> 00:01:55.736
and we always joke that
he's going to rescue Timmy

00:01:55.736 --> 00:01:58.004
from the well, so my dog got out again.

00:01:58.004 --> 00:01:59.693
(laughs) That's it.

00:01:59.693 --> 00:02:00.534
- [Voicemail] Hey Christian, yeah,

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.327
I figured since you're busy at work

00:02:02.327 --> 00:02:03.904
you probably wouldn't answer the phone,

00:02:03.904 --> 00:02:05.944
but I'm so thrilled about that article,

00:02:05.944 --> 00:02:09.777
so proud of you, very
proud, love you, bye!

00:02:11.844 --> 00:02:13.009
- Happy Mothers Day mom!

00:02:13.009 --> 00:02:13.870
- I love you mom!

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.054
- Happy Mothers Day mom.

00:02:15.054 --> 00:02:16.975
- Happy Mothers Day mom!

00:02:16.975 --> 00:02:19.808
(cheerful music)

